      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "Toronto's offseason exploded with purpose as the Maple Leafs, who limped home with a 78-point, 8th-place Atlantic finish and a crushing seven-game losing streak, refused to dwell on the past. The defining move arrived Wednesday: <strong>Sergei Bobrovsky agrees to a three-year, $21M deal</strong>, instantly rewriting the team's goaltending narrative after years of instability. GM John Chayka's roster overhaul didn't stop there - he added Colton Sissons, Jack Roslovic, Teddy Blueger, and Brandon Duhaime while trading Nick Robertson to Pittsburgh, signaling a blue-collar, depth-first rebuild. With Gavin McKenna now the franchise's first overall draft pick, the foundation is shifting toward grit and youth. <strong>What to watch next is how quickly Bobrovsky and McKenna integrate as the team aims to erase the L7 stigma and reclaim Atlantic dominance by next October.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 2, 2026"
      },
