      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Toronto Blue Jays didn't just beat the Mets - they exploded on Canada Day, a 9-3 rout that screamed <strong>Guerrero Jr. is finally showing signs of progress</strong> after a sluggish spring. That win, coupled with a 2-1 victory just two days prior, snapped a losing skid and gave the team its first W1 streak in weeks, even as they sit at 41-46, third in the AL East, and 11 games behind the division leader. The offense, which had been dormant for days, came alive with Guerrero leading the charge, while the pitching staff held firm in the tight 2-1 game. Injuries have been a quiet thorn, but the lineup's resurgence is the real story. <strong>Next up: a Saturday night showdown at Seattle's Mariners on 7/4 at 9:10 PM ET</strong>, where the Blue Jays must prove this isn't just a fluke but a turning point in their hunt.",
